<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1)) || (\old(this.get(i-1)) == null && this.get(i) == null));</code>

However, the above assertion is not quite correct as per the requirement. We need to ensure that the element at position `i+1` in the updated vector is equal to the element at position `i` in the old vector. Here is the corrected version:

<code>assert \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i));</code>

But we also need to handle the case where `index` is equal to the size of the vector, in which case no element is shifted up. So the correct assertion should be:

<code>assert \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i));</code>

And we should also ensure that the element at the `index` position in the new vector is the inserted element `obj`. So the complete assertion should be:

<code>assert this.get(index) == obj && \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i));</code>

Therefore, the final assert statement is:

<code>assert this.get(index) == obj && (\forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1) == \old(this.get(i)));</code>
